WEBVTT

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:10.880
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Thursday, seventh of May. Can you all hear me, or am I talking to myself again?</v>

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:20.309
<v Grace Liu>We can hear you. More importantly, there's a birthday cake in the office. Proper cake, not one of those protein things.</v>

00:00:20.929 --> 00:00:24.429
<v Callum Reid>That's the most useful production update we've had all week.</v>

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:33.700
<v Priya Raman>I'm hoping the weather holds for the weekend. Had grand plans for a walk, but the forecast's gone back to sideways rain.</v>

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:40.390
<v Marcus Hale>Standard bank holiday recovery weather. Back at work, sun comes out; weekend, absolutely buckets down.</v>

00:00:42.219 --> 00:00:45.369
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before we become the weather channel—what's already finished?</v>

00:00:47.399 --> 00:00:54.049
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, so, finished the repair on the line 2 last night. That's complete, not something I'm carrying into today.</v>

00:00:55.049 --> 00:00:58.899
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, we had that back. Much quieter on the radio afterwards.</v>

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:05.890
<v Priya Raman>And I finished the repair on the boiler last night as well. Both closed off.</v>

00:01:07.519 --> 00:01:12.420
<v Marcus Hale>Lovely. I saw the boiler entry, just hadn't heard the bit about line 2.</v>

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:19.000
<v Jamie Brennan>While we're on completed stuff, I already swapped the filter on the number two bearing yesterday.</v>

00:01:20.650 --> 00:01:23.799
<v Grace Liu>That's the bearing one, yeah? Not the compressed-air filter.</v>

00:01:25.849 --> 00:01:27.950
<v Jamie Brennan>Exactly. Separate thing. Yesterday's job, done.</v>

00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:31.560
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, the compressed-air filter is still outstanding, then.</v>

00:01:32.019 --> 00:01:36.920
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, Air Compressor 1. That's the one we're talking about, not the bearing filter.</v>

00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:44.390
<v Grace Liu>I'll swap the filter on the Air Compressor 1 by Thursday. It's urgent, so I'm taking that one.</v>

00:01:45.709 --> 00:01:48.859
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Grace Liu. Air Compressor 1 is yours, then.</v>

00:01:50.870 --> 00:01:53.670
<v Grace Liu>Yep. By Thursday means today, so we're clear.</v>

00:01:55.980 --> 00:02:02.980
<v Sarah Okafor>Jamie Brennan, can you do a site visit at the substation with the contractor by end of day? Normal priority.</v>

00:02:05.170 --> 00:02:11.120
<v Jamie Brennan>Sorry, no, I can't take that one. I'm not available to go out with the contractor today.</v>

00:02:12.199 --> 00:02:19.900
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, PR, can you take that instead—do a site visit at the substation with the contractor by end of day, normal priority?</v>

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:26.900
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, I'll take it. Site visit at the substation with the contractor, by end of day.</v>

00:02:28.879 --> 00:02:33.080
<v Marcus Hale>Sorry, I spoke over the end there. Was that still with Jamie?</v>

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:38.090
<v Priya Raman>No, with me. Normal priority, but still by end of day.</v>

00:02:39.969 --> 00:02:46.969
<v Jamie Brennan>One observation while I've got the mic: heard a slight rattle from the GT1 Compressor Section. Nothing to action yet.</v>

00:02:48.159 --> 00:02:53.759
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, just an observation at this point. Not a new job off the back of that.</v>

00:02:54.949 --> 00:02:59.500
<v Sarah Okafor>Separately, I'll grease and check the bearings on the GT1 compressor this morning.</v>

00:03:01.090 --> 00:03:04.939
<v Marcus Hale>Cheers, Saz. That's the bearing job, separate from Jamie's rattle comment.</v>

00:03:05.669 --> 00:03:09.870
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. I'm taking the grease and bearing check, not adding an investigation.</v>

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:14.949
<v Callum Reid>Production-wise, the guarding is the awkward one. That's where we're being held up.</v>

00:03:15.729 --> 00:03:24.129
<v Sarah Okafor>Hannah Price, can you check the guarding on the Main Outfeed Conveyor by the 28th? That's holding production up so it needs doing first.</v>

00:03:25.219 --> 00:03:31.169
<v Hannah Price>Yep, I'll check the guarding on the Main Outfeed Conveyor. By the 28th, and that goes first.</v>

00:03:32.939 --> 00:03:39.240
<v Callum Reid>Thanks. It's the order of work I was worried about, really, not just having a date against it.</v>

00:03:40.979 --> 00:03:44.129
<v Hannah Price>Understood. First, not squeezed in behind the routine stuff.</v>

00:03:44.710 --> 00:03:52.409
<v Sarah Okafor>And Hannah Price, can you update the risk assessment for work on the number two bearing by Thursday? That one's normal priority.</v>

00:03:53.439 --> 00:03:59.389
<v Hannah Price>Yes, I'll update the risk assessment for work on the number two bearing by Thursday. Normal priority.</v>

00:04:00.229 --> 00:04:05.830
<v Jamie Brennan>Just so we don't accidentally double it up, the filter swap I mentioned is already done.</v>

00:04:06.270 --> 00:04:10.469
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, understood. I'm taking the risk assessment update, not another filter swap.</v>

00:04:11.110 --> 00:04:17.410
<v Sarah Okafor>Hannah, can you also run a function test on the line 1 TCU on the 3rd? It's urgent.</v>

00:04:19.589 --> 00:04:25.540
<v Hannah Price>Okay, I'll run a function test on the line 1 TCU on the 3rd. Got the urgency.</v>

00:04:27.089 --> 00:04:32.339
<v Marcus Hale>That's a function test, rather than calibration? Sorry, Teams clipped the first couple of words.</v>

00:04:34.629 --> 00:04:37.079
<v Hannah Price>Function test, yeah. Not a calibration job.</v>

00:04:38.269 --> 00:04:44.920
<v Sarah Okafor>The calibration is separate. Jamie Brennan, can you recalibrate the sensors on the air dryer by Wednesday? Normal priority.</v>

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:53.110
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, I can take that. I'll recalibrate the sensors on the air dryer by Wednesday, normal priority.</v>

00:04:54.040 --> 00:05:00.339
<v Priya Raman>Right, air dryer sensors with Jamie, function test on the line 1 TCU with Hannah. Two different things.</v>

00:05:02.449 --> 00:05:06.300
<v Jamie Brennan>That's it. Heard air dryer clearly, even through this lovely headset.</v>

00:05:07.980 --> 00:05:11.480
<v Hannah Price>Oh, and I'll send the shift handover report round tomorrow.</v>

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:15.800
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Hannah. Tomorrow for the shift handover report.</v>

00:05:17.129 --> 00:05:19.579
<v Hannah Price>Yep. Saves everyone wondering where it is.</v>

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:25.610
<v Sarah Okafor>Any blocked or deferred stuff we need to keep separate from those commitments?</v>

00:05:27.019 --> 00:05:35.769
<v Jamie Brennan>Can't get to the Stretch Wrapper until production gives us a window. Still blocked, so I'm not taking that on as a job for today.</v>

00:05:36.569 --> 00:05:40.069
<v Callum Reid>There's no window available at the minute. Nothing's changed there.</v>

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:47.139
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay. Stretch Wrapper stays blocked. No action coming out of this meeting on that.</v>

00:05:49.069 --> 00:05:57.120
<v Jamie Brennan>And we were going to replace the belt on the boiler feed pump, but that's been pushed to next month, so ignore it.</v>

00:05:57.439 --> 00:06:00.939
<v Marcus Hale>Right, so that hasn't quietly crept back onto today's list.</v>

00:06:02.600 --> 00:06:06.100
<v Sarah Okafor>No. Deferred to next month, not being handed out today.</v>

00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:12.410
<v Grace Liu>Good. The cake, on the other hand, is definitely available today. No production window required.</v>

00:06:13.689 --> 00:06:16.839
<v Jamie Brennan>Depends how wide the queue outside the office is.</v>

00:06:18.660 --> 00:06:23.209
<v Priya Raman>Still a better prospect than my weekend picnic, by the sound of it.</v>

00:06:24.149 --> 00:06:35.350
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. Just to keep the priorities straight: Main Outfeed Conveyor guarding first because it's holding production up. Air Compressor 1 is urgent, and the line 1 TCU function test is urgent too.</v>

00:06:37.389 --> 00:06:42.639
<v Hannah Price>Yep, I've got that. Guarding first, and the dates on my other bits as agreed.</v>

00:06:44.819 --> 00:06:48.319
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely. That's everyone. Thanks all, I'll let you get on.</v>
